# Cookbook: Deploying an application

This recipe deploys `myapp`, a service shipped as a tarball, and keeps it running. It sets up:

- a system account and a private state directory;
- each release unpacked into a directory of its own, with a symlink to the active one;
- a configuration file rendered from a template;
- a systemd unit that runs the service as its account, with restrictions;
- a restart whenever the release or the configuration changes.

Upgrading is then `terraform apply -var app_version=1.5.0`, and the plan shows exactly what the upgrade changes. This recipe uses [`sysutils_archive_extract`](../resources/archive_extract.md), [`sysutils_symlink`](../resources/symlink.md), [`sysutils_template_file`](../resources/template_file.md), [`sysutils_systemd_unit`](../resources/systemd_unit.md) and [`sysutils_service`](../resources/service.md). It requires root and systemd.

The complete configuration is in [`examples/guides/app-deployment`](https://github.com/blechschmidt/terraform-provider-sysutils/tree/main/examples/guides/app-deployment). It includes a stand-in tarball, so you can apply it as it is on a test machine.

